/-!
# The Laurent phenomenon (wanted)

The Laurent phenomenon of Fomin and Zelevinsky for coefficient-free seed patterns.

The ambient field is `ℚ(x_i : i ∈ n)`, realised as `FractionRing (MvPolynomial n ℤ)` with the
initial cluster `x_i = X_i`. The ring of Laurent polynomials `ℤ[x_i^{±1}]` is the `ℤ`-subalgebra
generated by the `x_i` and their inverses. These definitions, `initialCluster` and
`laurentSubalgebra`, and the rank-two case `rankTwoSeq_mem_laurentSubalgebra` are in
`MathlibExt.RingTheory.ClusterAlgebra.LaurentPhenomenon`.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.RingTheory.ClusterAlgebra.LaurentPhenomenonWanted

open MathlibExt.RingTheory.ClusterAlgebra

/-- **Laurent phenomenon (coefficient-free).** Let `B` be a skew-symmetrizable integer
`n × n` matrix and start from the seed `((X_i), B)` in `ℚ(X_i : i ∈ n)`. Every cluster variable
of every seed obtained by iterated mutation is a Laurent polynomial in the `X_i` with integer
coefficients (Fomin, Williams and Zelevinsky, *Introduction to cluster algebras, Chapters 1–3*,
arXiv:1608.05735v5, Theorem 3.3.1, in the case without frozen variables; Fomin and
Zelevinsky, *Cluster algebras I*, J. Amer. Math. Soc. 15 (2002), Theorem 3.1). The source
theorem also allows frozen variables and expands in every extended cluster; this statement is
the coefficient-free case, relative to the initial cluster, which by relabelling the initial seed
covers expansions in any cluster of the pattern. -/
theorem_wanted laurent_phenomenon {n : Type*} [Fintype n] [DecidableEq n]
    (B : Matrix n n ℤ) (hB : IsSkewSymmetrizable B) (w : List n) (i : n) :
    (mutateSeq w (initialCluster n, B)).1 i ∈ laurentSubalgebra n

end MathlibExt.RingTheory.ClusterAlgebra.LaurentPhenomenonWanted
